  "why": "The platform cache and --no-platform-cache exist now; this re-measures the gap the 09:00Z smoke showed (9.0 s cold vs Go 0.16 s). Measured in a worktree at 1235dc4b8a68 with the release-built flint and DMD linking with mold (ADR-021); the cache is primed by one recorded, unscored build. About 20 minutes, so it fits a short window. Re-pinned for m7-flint-cli's 19390bd1 (Flint AOT's platform modules as a cached library) and cc2f98e2 (stat-keyed digests). Re-pinned for m7-flint-cli's ff31b6d2: the generated AOT library (Boot's auto-configuration modules, including the 0.45 s Jackson module) is cached in the platform cache and linked on a cached cold build; the receipt lists it as flint-aot-library. The certified 12:30Z run stays in 'attempts'. Re-pinned for 592d4b37: the dev build links the platform cache as a shared object (primary edit-build headline) and --static gives the fully static secondary (owner decision 2). Re-pinned for dmd-arm64's compile-server platform prelude (42ebbef9, 0d0d3afd): the checkout builds its own DMD fork from its patch ('fork'). Re-pinned for d2a929cd: the receipt's phases_ms gives per-phase medians. Re-pinned for m7-flint-cli's c2ae7990: the platform description (dub describe and its parse) is cached in the project, so an edit build skips both (phases_ms.flint 72 to 26 ms locally); cold trials clear .flint and describe again, as before. It also includes dmd-arm64's prelude (0d0d3afd). Re-pinned for m7-flint-cli's 2018e5e5: the description record ignores unrelated environment and fork patches use the digest cache; with flint-aot's 2cd5ce4d, flint's own edit-build phase is at about its 20 ms budget locally, so the per-phase medians show it against that budget. Re-pinned at 1235dc4b8a68 for m7-flint-cli's bf7b7b97 (DUB's plan off the shared dev edit path: flint runs DUB's compile and link itself; FLINT_DIRECT_BUILD=0 restores DUB) and the digest-log method of decisions.md 2026-11-23 17:00Z (cached cold trials keep the platform digest log; the cleared series is context).",
